<title>USA: U.S. Q4 corporate profits rose 1.5 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q4 corporate profits rose 1.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department estimates of fourth quarter profits by U.S. corporations, with comparisons. Profits before tax include inventory valuation and capital consumption adjustments.</p>
<p>Data are chain weighted and expressed in seasonally adjusted annual rates of billions of dollars, with third quarter percent changes from the second quarter.</p>
<p> -		   Pct--Q4'96--Q3'96--Q2'96---1996</p>
<p> -  After Tax    1.5  408.2  402.2  408.1  406.8</p>
<p> -  Before Tax  -1.1  654.1  661.2  655.8  654.0</p>
<p> Tax Liability  -1.9  228.9  233.4  236.4  233.0</p>
</text>
